# Python virtual environment — never commit this, it's machine-specific and huge
.venv/
venv/

# Geospatial datasets — the ORIGINAL raw government files are too large for a
# normal git repo (wris_rivers.parquet alone is ~150MB, over GitHub's 100MB
# per-file hard limit). Download instructions for these raw files are in
# README.md. They are NOT needed to run the app or deploy to Render — only to
# regenerate the small files below via preprocess_geo_data.py.
#
# The small *_simplified.parquet / esz_reprojected.parquet / *_simplified.geojson
# files ARE committed (they're what geo_classifier.py actually loads, ~40MB
# total combined) — see geo_classifier.py's memory notes for why. Only the
# raw originals are excluded below, by exact filename.
Coastline/india_boundary.geojson
Ecosensitive zone/Bharatmaps_Parivesh_Eco_Sensitive_Zones.parquet
Ecosensitive zone/Bharatmaps_Parivesh_Eco_Sensitive_Zones.geojson
Flood+ Innundation/ndem_floods_1998_2022.parquet
Protected Areas/GatiShakti_Wildlife_Sanctuaries_and_National_Parks.parquet
Rivers+ Streams/wris_rivers.parquet
